</style>
<div class="ev-static"><table class="ev-table"><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th align="center">Int</th><th align="center">§</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="#app-conjure-air">Conjure Air</a></td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">§2B1</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-dormitive-vapours">Dormitive Vapours</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§2A5</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-remove-air">Remove Air</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§2B2</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-create-smoke">Create Smoke</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§2B3</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-stinging-vapours">Stinging Vapours</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§2B4</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-sustenance">Sustenance</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§2B6</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-protection-from-air">Protection from Air</a></td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">§2B7</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-alter-weather">Alter Weather</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§2A10</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-cone-of-heat">Cone of Heat</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§2A8</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-poisonous-vapours">Poisonous Vapours</a></td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">§2A9</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-summon-air-elemental">Summon Air Elemental</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§2A11</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#app-lightning-bolt">Lightning Bolt</a></td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">§2A12</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="ev-cards"><section class="ev-card" id="app-conjure-air"><h3>Conjure Air</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2B1</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Create a 5m×5m×5m volume of air in a space perhaps already occupied by air or vapour (but nothing denser). This volume may be decreased, but the air may not be compressed further.

Used judiciously, this spell creates gusts of wind, etc. (<strong>immediate</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-dormitive-vapours"><h3>Dormitive Vapours</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2A5</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Create a volume of anaesthetic vapour occupying a volume 1m×1m×1m (<strong>fixed</strong>).

Inhalers must make an EF=5 WP roll to resist falling asleep, and remain asleep until the gas disperses and the inhaler has regained reserve fatigue levels, or is shaken awake.

Note: a character or creature whose fatigue is already at or above reserve fatigue will only remain asleep until the gas disperses or he/she is shaken awake.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-remove-air"><h3>Remove Air</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2B2</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Remove all the air or vapour from a 2m×2m×2m volume (<strong>immediate</strong>). This won't suffocate people, but it can produce thunderclaps, slam doors, etc.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-create-smoke"><h3>Create Smoke</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2B3</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Create a volume of thick smoke occupying a volume 5m×5m×5m (<strong>fixed</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-stinging-vapours"><h3>Stinging Vapours</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2B4</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Create a volume of irritating gas (equivalent to tear gas) occupying a volume 2m×2m×2m (<strong>fixed</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-sustenance"><h3>Sustenance</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2B6</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The invoker may render him/herself, or one recipient, capable of surviving in a hostile (or lacking) atmosphere for the duration of the spell (<strong>controlled, bestowed</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-protection-from-air"><h3>Protection from Air</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2B7</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The invoker may render him/herself or another more resistant to attacks which damage through heat or moistening, by reducing the DCs of said attacks by 4.

If the attack damages through one of the two, and something else (eg. drying, like a fire-based attack), then this protection drops to a reduction in DC of 2.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-alter-weather"><h3>Alter Weather</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2A10</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Alter the weather within a 1km radius by shifting the weather's description by one row on each of the three columns below.

While the duration of this effect is only two minutes, the return to normality will be gradual (as though the artificially invoked conditions had come about naturally).

| Temperature | Wind<em> | Precipitation |
|---|---|---|
| -50°C | Calm | None |
| -30°C | Slight Breeze | Fog |
| -10°C | Gusty Breeze | Drizzle |
| 5°C | Moderate Wind | Medium Rain |
| 20°C | Strong Wind | Heavy Rain |
| 30°C | Storm Wind | Rivers Flood Levies |
| 40°C | Gale | Flash Floods |
| 50°C | Hurricane | (Or hail or snow if applicable) |
| 60°C | Tornado | |

Note: </em> Wind direction may be altered by up to 45° (eg. from SE to E) instead of altering its intensity.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-cone-of-heat"><h3>Cone of Heat</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2A8</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The invoker may create a cone of heat with its base anywhere within range. The cone is 20m wide at its base and draws to a point at its invoker. Those wholly or mostly within it suffer <strong>DC3</strong> from heat (<strong>immediate</strong>).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-poisonous-vapours"><h3>Poisonous Vapours</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>2</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2A9</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Create a volume of poisonous vapour occupying a volume 1m×1m×1m (<strong>fixed</strong>).

Those breathing the gas must successfully perform a PR roll or suffer one point of damage each pulse thereafter, until achieving a QR1 or 2 on one of the pain resistance rolls.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-summon-air-elemental"><h3>Summon Air Elemental</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2A11</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Summon an elemental of air (<strong>controlled</strong>). The elemental appears in 2×(QR-1) pulses. See [5.2].</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-lightning-bolt"><h3>Lightning Bolt</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>3</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§2A12</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>air</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">Create a lightning bolt 1m wide extending from the invoker to a point within range (<strong>immediate</strong>).

Anyone touched by the lightning bolt, or placed in electrical contact with it, takes <strong>DC6</strong> and is automatically stunned. If he/she achieves a QR10 on his/her PR roll (for the damage) he/she dies of heart failure, and must be revived by a skilled person (at least if in low-tech surroundings) within a minute.

A lightning bolt damages through heat and moisture.</p></section></div></div>
</div>
<!-- /magic-apps -->

# Apportation
<!--{ "parent": "magic", "order": 3 }-->

*move objects at a distance; magical transport*

A **Fundamental** — a Field of Magical Knowledge whose applications reach **50m** and last **10min**; the usual props are **a pole, or a glove**. Learn it **Basic** (1 yr) for the easy end, **Advanced** (3 yr) for the deep.

Its **15 applications**, by intensity:

<!-- magic-apps: Apportation -->
