Note: the GM can either make a best guess as to the demeanours of PCs, ask their players for an honest opinion, or simply exclude them from this application's effects.</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-telepathic-dialogue"><h3>Telepathic Dialogue</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>4</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§5A8</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>communication</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The invoker may engage in telepathic dialogue with any target within range.

If used by the leader of a party in combat, the leader gains a +2 to Initiative rolls (able to quickly and accurately receive information and give orders).

Any lies made during telepathic dialogue are detected if the person lied to makes an Empathy roll (Silvertongue notwithstanding).</p></section><section class="ev-card" id="app-telepathic-probe"><h3>Telepathic Probe</h3><dl class="ev-fields"><dt>Intensity</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Code</dt><dd>§5A9</dd><dt>Source</dt><dd>communication</dd></dl><p class="ev-body">The invoker may telepathically probe the mind of any one subject within range, and can locate any mind within range.

While concentrating on the thoughts of another, the invoker may not, him/herself, perform any actions whatsoever.

The invoker can:

- read the verbal thoughts of the subject (regardless of language, but no good for non-verbally minded creatures, unless the invoker is one);
- sense what the subject is sensing (sight, sound, touch, etc.);
- sense the emotional state of the subject.

The invoker cannot in any way control the subject, or search through the subject's memories. !!!</p></section></div></div>
